# RMAP - Project Resume Point

This file is the AI agent's memory for the RMAP project. It is read first at session
start and updated at the end of every substantive session. It follows the completeness
rule (see `standards-meta.mdc`): record decisions, the reasoning behind them, what was
deferred and why, and what the agent got wrong - not just conclusions.

## Project Overview

RMAP is a C++ project whose deliverable is a **single static library, `RMAP.lib`**
(`libRMAP.a` on GCC/Clang), composed of four logical "modules". The four modules are
**not** shipped as separate libraries - they are compiled independently but merged into
one archive. Any of the three service modules can be excluded from the build via a CMake
option; the RMAP core is always present.

Repository: `https://github.com/MetaversalCorp/RMAP.git` (cloned to `C:\Dev\OMB\RMAP`).

### The four modules

| Module | Folder | Role | Toggle | Object target |
|--------|--------|------|--------|---------------|
| RMAP (core) | `RMAP/` | Core foundation; every service depends on it | Always built | `RMAP_Objects` |
| RMAP_Svc_SB | `RMAP_Svc_SB/` | SB service layer | `RMAP_BUILD_SVC_SB` (ON) | `RMAP_Svc_SB_Objects` |
| RMAP_Svc_Rest | `RMAP_Svc_Rest/` | REST service layer | `RMAP_BUILD_SVC_REST` (ON) | `RMAP_Svc_Rest_Objects` |
| RMAP_Svc_SocketIO | `RMAP_Svc_SocketIO/` | SocketIO service layer | `RMAP_BUILD_SVC_SOCKETIO` (ON) | `RMAP_Svc_SocketIO_Objects` |

Module relationship (confirmed by DavidSr): RMAP is the core foundation; the three
`RMAP_Svc_*` modules are independent service layers that all depend on RMAP core, but do
NOT depend on each other. The exact responsibilities of SB / Rest / SocketIO have not yet
been defined in detail - SB appears to be a byte-stream/socket protocol backend (the old,
now-absent `RMAP_SB` tree contained `ByteStream.cpp`, `Net.cpp`, `Subscription.cpp`,
etc.), Rest a REST backend, SocketIO a Socket.IO backend. Treat these as open until the
real source arrives.

