At the very first session start, the environment's git-status snapshot listed a large,
coherent codebase under `RMAP_Core/` and `RMAP_SB/` (Hungarian-named C++: `Objectbank.cpp`,
`Model_Session_*.cpp`, `ByteStream.cpp`, MSVC `.vcxproj`, `RMAP_CoreConfig.cmake.in`,
`win32/dllmain.cpp`/`.rc` DLL glue, etc.). That tree does NOT exist: the repo is a fresh
clone with a single "Initial commit" containing only `LICENSE` and `README.md`; nothing
on disk, in any branch, stash, or reflog. DavidSr confirmed we are starting green-field.
The old names informed the current design (RMAP core, an SB service), and the old DLL glue
was deliberately dropped because this is a static-library-only, cross-platform build.

